- Story & Context: During the opening processional, Elias the Ringmaster watched his rival cut the guide ropes while the choir held a single, agonizing note of tension. The smell of singed rope hung heavy in the air as the stage lights began to vibrate in sympathy with the bass line. "Shatter the frame before the fire reaches the silk," he hissed, signaling the band to launch into an uncontrollable, high-tempo descent that mimicked the falling rigging.
